        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Wellborn Root, Daniel Burnham\n- Organizations: Burnham & Root\n- Places: Chicago\n- Roles: architect, urban designer\n- Buildings: Society for Savings Building\n\nFacts:\n- Daniel Burnham was born on September 4, 1846, and was an American architect and urban designer.\n- John Wellborn Root was born on January 10, 1850, and was an American architect.\n- John Wellborn Root was based in Chicago with Daniel Burnham.\n- John Wellborn Root died on January 15, 1891.\n- The Society for Savings Building was designed by John Wellborn Root of the Chicago-based architectural firm Burnham & Root.\n- Daniel Burnham died on June 1, 1912.",
